WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.810
Let's go next to let's go to Mohammed from
Qatar.

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:02.810
I don't believe we've ever had a call from
Qatar before.

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:03.810
Mohammed, what's on your mind?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.810
Mohamed, you have to unmuted if you want me
to be able to hear you.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:05.810
Mohammed from Qatar, I would love for you
to be the first Qatari caller, but that's

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:06.810
probably not going to happen the way things
are looking.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:07.810
All right, no Mohammed from Qatar, that's
too bad.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:08.810
That's too bad.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.810
I was really looking forward to that.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:10.810
Let's go to or from Milwaukee, Wisconsin.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.810
David, can you hear me?

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:12.810
Yes, I can.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:13.810
Oh, great.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:14.810
Thank you again for taking my call.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.160
I just wanted to talk a little bit about,
I guess, the student loans and the crisis

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.160
that's going on with that.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.970
Clearly, the Biden administration and congressional
Democrats are aiming at canceling some form

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:27.380
of back, whether that be five thousand to
fifty thousand.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.380
Yep.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.780
It seems that there are some subsector of
of America that is a little bit hesitant to

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.120
it for various reasons, whether that be paying
them down already or not having it in the

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.059
first place, although it does seem that the
majority of Americans do support that.

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:46.600
And I guess my question would be, how do we
address that?

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.800
Would there possibly be in the long term versus
just obviously clearly.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.629
Canceling some portion of that debt is going
to alleviate some of the issue in the short

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:02.690
term, but the long term, it seems to me that
predatory loans are maybe more of the issue

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.409
rather than the actual.

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:05.409
Yep.

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:08.180
So here's here's my view.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.030
Because of if we were rebuilding the system
from scratch, we would just build it in a

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.030
different way.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:17.940
That would prevent the cycle of it's so easy
to get student loans, which makes it easy

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.649
for colleges to raise prices because then
you just get the loans and then you owe more

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.649
money.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:26.079
But wages don't go up and it becomes unsustainable,
which is what we have.

00:01:26.079 --> 00:01:27.109
That's the crisis that we have.

00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:28.680
We would build the system differently.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:36.689
But being that we are where we are, there
should be some degree of student loan forgiveness.

00:01:36.689 --> 00:01:40.410
And I've seen a lot of different proposals
about what that should be and how it should

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.410
be targeted.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:45.979
As I've said before, it doesn't strike me
that the right way to do it is to forgive

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:48.079
every dollar of student debt for everybody.

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:54.969
That doesn't make sense to me, but I think
that some fixed amount plus more with certain

00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:59.299
requirements attached to it is a good way
to go.

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:04.330
But you're completely right that that doesn't
really solve the problem, because if you just

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:08.730
have a policy of we forgive everyone's loans
forever, then schools just keep making school

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.110
more expensive and, you know, the cycle essentially
continues.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:17.270
So I think you kind of get back into the same
cycle where, you know, we're going to wipe

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.870
the slate clean, but then we haven't really
address the root issue of the problem.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:28.740
Exactly what I'm thinking in my head is it
doesn't make sense to maybe go with or establish

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:35.200
some sort of a federal loan program where
there is a little to no interest rate lower

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.290
or providing federal dollars as a loan.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:42.060
So that exists already that that exists already
for grad school.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:48.980
I had I had the federal loans where interest
accrual is suspended for periods of time.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.200
And so so that that exists, it could be expanded.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.530
I think ultimately something needs to be done
to bring the cost of college in line with

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.020
with wages.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:03.780
Because if you look at how the cost of college
has changed relative to wages in many fields,

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.120
it's completely out of whack.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.030
If you look at cost of college relative to
inflation, relative to cost of living, it's

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.250
completely out of whack.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.420
So that's what needs to be gotten under control.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:18.760
I'm not saying the government just needs to
decide what prices are that does that.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.240
You know, I don't think that that's the solution.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.980
Government sets prices on private and public
schooling, but something needs to get done,

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.320
be done to reign to get that under control.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.230
And the student loan piece is a problem that
subsidizes colleges continuing to charge more

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.230
and more.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:40.260
And a one time debt forgiveness is not going
to deal with that issue.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:41.260
All right.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.260
Well, thanks again for taking my call.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.260
I really appreciate it.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.260
My pleasure.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:45.720
Very important issue or I appreciate the call.

